  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only configuration so far is config_005 (scVI n200, multiprofile, avgpool) at 0.650 acc / 0.628 F1, clearly outperforming PCA (0.591) and transformer aggregation (0.519). The encoder choice (scVI vs PCA) and aggregation choice (avgpool vs transformer) are both well-supported. However, scGPT is an entirely untested encoder, and we have no evidence about whether it could surpass scVI. Question: config_008 (scGPT, multiprofile, avgpool) isolates the encoder effect by holding profile setting and aggregation fixed at their best-performing values, enabling a direct A/B comparison against config_005. Why this is the best next experiment: Under a limited budget, identifying whether a superior encoder exists is the highest-leverage uncertainty to resolve. If scGPT matches or beats scVI, it opens a new design axis; if it underperforms, we can confidently commit to scVI and shift exploration toward fusion or image-encoder questions. This single experiment reduces uncertainty about the most important remaining design choice on the RNA side without changing multiple variables simultaneously."
}

